# SPA page shell (Lock 1)

Every operational screen uses this stack inside its root (sibling order):

1. `PageHeader` — the page's single `<h1>` (Title Case strings; never `mode.replace` or route keys). Room Plan and Front Desk boards may put `CountStrip` counts in `PageHeader` `lead` (inline with the title).
2. Optional `Tabs` / control row / sibling KPI above the card.
3. `Card` with optional `Toolbar`, `CardHeader` + `CardTitle` (`<h2>` section title only), `CardContent`.

`PageHeader` is a **sibling above** `Card`, not inside `CardHeader`.

## Caller classNames (ui-kit router contract)

- View tabs: host `<Link className="ui-tab" aria-current="page">` on the active tab.
- Navigable KPIs: host `<Link className="ui-metric">` (Dashboard cards) or `<Link className="ui-count">` (CountStrip on Room Plan / boards).
- Choice rows: each option is `<li className="ui-choice-row"><label className="ui-choice">` (vertical list; radio beside label on one baseline).

Do not add `className` to closed ui-kit components except `Card`'s existing leak. **Allowed ui-kit extension:** `CardContent flush?: boolean`.

## Tape (Room Plan)

- Half-day grid: `--tape-room-w: 6.5rem`, `--tape-day-min: 4rem`; columns `var(--tape-room-w) repeat(calc(var(--tape-cols) * 2), minmax(calc(var(--tape-day-min) / 2), 1fr))`. Inline style sets only `--tape-cols`, `--tape-col-start`, `--tape-col-end` (and legacy `--tape-col` if needed).
- `.tape-scroller` must include `max-block-size` using the Room Plan calc (`100dvh` minus top bar, band reserve, side panels, room-plan padding/gaps/header/controls). The check script only asserts that `.tape-scroller` has `max-block-size`.
- Sticky head and free rows use `--table-head`; room-type band is 20px inside the scroller.
- One scrollport: `.main:has(.room-plan)` does not scroll; `.tape-scroller` does.

## Housekeeping host

`HousekeepingScreen.tsx` is a thin host only — **do not** add `PageHeader`/`Card` there. Chrome lives in `modules/pms/housekeeping/src/ui/HousekeepingApp.tsx`.

## Enforcement

Merge-blocking: `pnpm check:spa-page-chrome` (live) + `node scripts/spa-page-chrome-check.mjs --self-test`. Do not invent a third card padding scheme — use `CardContent flush` for table/tape bodies.
